Subject: Re: kickoff — realtime outputs + function calls

Alex / team —

Good questions — short answers and a sample schema below.

- Correlation: include a session_id + request_id when you start a stream. For webhook replies from function calls, Redwood will attach the same request_id so you can join events client-side.
- final_token_index: yes — when we emit the final structured output we populate a control field metadata.final_token_index that points to the token offset inside the overall stream.

Sample structured output schema (minimal example you can validate quickly):

{
  "$schema": "http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#",
  "title": "clinical_note_output",
  "type": "object",
  "properties": {
    "session_id": {"type": "string"},
    "request_id": {"type": "string"},
    "final_token_index": {"type": "integer"},
    "patient": {
      "type": "object",
      "properties": {
        "patient_id": {"type": "string"},
        "dob": {"type": "string", "format": "date"}
      },
      "required": ["patient_id"]
    },
    "observations": {
      "type": "array",
      "items": {
        "type": "object",
        "properties": {
          "type": {"type": "string"},
          "value": {"type": "string"},
          "confidence": {"type": "number", "minimum": 0, "maximum": 1}
        },
        "required": ["type","value"]
      }
    },
    "metadata": {
      "type": "object",
      "properties": {
        "generated_by": {"type": "string"},
        "timestamp": {"type": "string", "format": "date-time"}
      }
    }
  },
  "required": ["session_id","request_id","patient","observations"]
}

We'll include this as structured-output-schema-example.json in the drive as well. For the kickoff, please upload 3 real-ish test payloads (anonymized) so we can run validation and end-to-end streaming tests.

See you at 10am PT.

—Stephanie
